statement       : A beneficiary of an estate is entitled to sue for their share without obtaining letters.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1929-50-1
statement       : An executor who has applied to the court for and obtained an order for the sale of immovable 
                  property has no authority to dispose of the property except upon further orders of the court.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1936-47-1
statement       : The recitals in a deed prevail over the operative part if the recitals are clear while the operative 
                  part is not clear.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1937-88-1
statement       : A husband has the same right to mortgage property forming part of the thediathetam property after 
                  the passing of Ordinance No. 1 of 1911 as he had before its enactment.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1945-21-1
statement       : Order 22 Rule 10 can apply to parties other than plaintiffs and their representatives.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1946-67-1
statement       : A bona fide purchaser from a defendant who obtained a decree through misrepresentation or fraud is 
                  entitled to rely on the vendor's title.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1950-18-1
statement       : A joint affirmative injury inflicted by multiple defendants constitutes one cause of action.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1950-18-2
statement       : This case is not explicitly mentioned in the HELD passage.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1950-18-3
statement       : A party cannot unilaterally withdraw an action once it has been dismissed.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1950-77-1
statement       : The court cannot infer that a person was a cultivator prior to taking a usufructuary mortgage bond 
                  based on the absence of evidence.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1950-77-2
statement       : A tenant's rights can be extinguished through surrender or through both surrender and merger.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1950-77-3
statement       : Surrender of a contract of tenancy occurs when the parties perform an act inconsistent with their 
                  landlord-tenant relationship.
statute_section : 

rule_id         : draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1951-16-1
statement       : In an action for declaration of title to the office of Viharadhipathi, the action can be continued 
                  by or against the successor-in-title.
statute_section : 

